Z||000004||Ed||12-22-1999||08:39 PM||||Don't get too excited about sunroof parts. After reading the post, I went to my dealer today with the part number. Tabs are "no longer available." If you can get one for me I'll take it! ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||10:21 PM||||Don't let your dealer lie to you.  They are still available.  I just got mine 2 weeks ago.  If your dealer refuses to order them for you, let me know.  I can get them and send them to you COD.  They are $13US for both tabs and both plastic washers.  You might need to go to a Pontiac dealer.  My local dealer (sounds like that drug thing, again) is Chevy, Pontiac and Oldsmobile.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||12-24-1999||05:28 PM||||I just bought two yesterday. If you continue to get those types of answers, find another dealer. I've been buy parts that many people here say are no available.<P>Also, find a parts department that is in the most run down building you can find. Usually, this means they aren't paying for the crystal cathedral show room and the prices are cheaper. <P>The list price for parts are not set by GM. Two different parts departments will quote two different "list prices". Where I by my parts, the list price is cheaper than the "discount price" quoted at the auto mall. With the discounts, the prices are excellent. The tabs were $9.25.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||12-24-1999||07:54 PM||||You should also complian to 1800PMCARES and anyone else at GM that will listen. They don't like it much if their dealers are making them look bad. It can affect the contract the dealer gets next time it's due.||||reg||1
